@misc{Łukawski_24205,
 abstract = {Posthuman Creativity Labs: Artificial Intelligence and Blockchain in Music (2 ECTS)
Level: for BA (2nd & 3rd year) and MA students
Form of study: face-to-face learning (seminars + workshops)
Course description:
Through seminars and practical workshops this course focussed on how existing AI (Artificial Intelligence) and blockchain tools can enhance the creative capabilities of a musician today and how this changes the creative practices that we know. The aim was to provide to participants the basic knowledge about the new paradigms of (digital) art creation and dissemination and to navigate them towards the digital tools enabling post-human creativity to become part of their own artistic practice. Some of the questions that the course strived to answer are: how can human creativity be enhanced by Artificial Intelligence? What are the good techniques for music composition with AI and blockchain? How is the definition of a work of art different today than 300 years ago and 100 years ago? What is the purpose of decentralised music? What is the agency of the work of art in the post-human era? Can the work of art posses itself?

Learning outcomes: 
- Understanding of how AI and blockchain technologies can augment and
redefine the creative processes in music.
- Understanding the potential of these digital tools in shaping post-human artistic practices.
- Understanding of the theororetical framework surrounding these technologies.
- Being able to support their own artistic practice with aforementioned tools and technologies.},
